━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Loops is facet of FunctionEmitter
    sees Cleanups
    sees LiveActions
    sees MatchArms
    sees Streams
    sees Tables

────────────────────
+ do emit-while
    - id SyntaxId
    - condition SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A loop that runs its body for as long as its condition tests as true. Each pass polls
` before the test. The loop is one to leave or to go on with from its condition on: written
` with a pattern, its body runs in the arm of the match that is the condition. A turn
` whose locals nested functions capture has an environment of its own. A condition that
` opens a cleanup, reading a lazy local whose value is a `use`, has no shape: TypeScript
` runs that cleanup where the body ends, and not at all where the condition first fails.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. head = ir.reserve-block()
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
jump(head)
ir.start-block(head)
emit-poll(id)
. open = open-cleanups.length
loops += EmittedLoop(id, head, done, nothing, no-type, open, no-slot)
branch-on(condition, inside, done)
if open-cleanups.length != open
    refuse(.refused-expression, condition)
ir.start-block(inside)
. turns = open-turns.length
open-turn(id, nothing, no-type)
emit-block(body)
close-turns(turns)
loops.pop()
jump(head)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
+ do emit-for
    - id SyntaxId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A loop over items, run as the type pass planned it: one that counts through a range of
` integers written in its header, or one over the container of each of its headers. One on a
` stream subscribes where it is written, and runs for an item in the function generated for
` it.
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop) == .plan-range-loop
            do match? tree.nodes[row.container]
                | .node-range-expression(range)
                    emit-range-loop(loop, range.op, range.left, range.right, row.clause, body)
                    =
        else if !row.is-subscriber
            emit-headed(loop, row.container, row.clause, body)
            =
        else if subscribing == id
            emit-subscriber(loop, tested(loop, row.clause), body)
            =
        else
            emit-subscription(id, loop, row.container)
            =
refuse(.refused-statement, id)

────────────────────
+ do hold-container TypeId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - kept Bool = false

` Evaluates the container of a loop, once, and keeps it in the first of the loop's slots,
` converted as the type pass recorded where it is written, and answers its type. The loop of
` a comprehension keeps its container already: the function generated for it was given the
` container where it was called. So does the loop of a bullet, which kept it where the bullet
` began, as `kept` says.
holding = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop) == .plan-table-loop && kept
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = no-type
if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop) == .plan-table-loop
    = hold-rows(loop, container, slot)
if loop == given-loop || kept
    . kept = state(slot, loop)
    holding = kept.operand
    = kept.type
if reads-place(loop)
    . base = facts.loop-base(unit.reading, loop)
    if base == U32.max
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
        = no-type
    if base != 0
        . object = emit-expression(base)
        pin(base, object.operand, object.type)
    . emitted = emit-expression(container)
    if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout-of(emitted.type, loop))
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = emitted.type
. held = convert(container, .reason-operand, emit-expression(container))
. type = held.type
keep-state(slot, held.operand, type, loop)
holding = held.operand
= type

────────────────────
_ do hold-rows TypeId
    - loop SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` Begins a loop over a table or a span of one, as TypeScript begins it: the container is
` evaluated, once, and its rows found, checked where the table grows; the first row is kept,
` and the count of rows. An index span is kept, and its length. Answers the container's type.
` The loop of a comprehension reads the container it was given from the slot after its item.
. table = if loop == given-loop then state(slot + loop-state-count, loop) else convert(container, .reason-operand, emit-expression(container))
. type = table.type
if intrinsic(type) == .table-selection || intrinsic(type) == .immutable-table-selection
    hold-selection(loop, table.operand, type, slot)
    = type
if intrinsic(type) == .index-span
    . layout = layout-of(type, loop)
    keep-state(slot, table.operand, type, loop)
    keep-state(slot + 1, word-at(loop, table.operand, layout, 3), types.size-type, loop)
    = type
. offset = slot-offset(slot, loop)
. row = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset)
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
. row-layout = layout-of(row, loop)
. source = table-source(loop, table.operand, type, layout)
. made = frame(row-layout)
if is-immutable-view(intrinsic(type))
    put
        - made
        - tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 0)
        - num-cast(loop, source.columns, pointer-layout, managed-layout)
        - loop
    put(made, tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 1), source.offset, loop)
else
    put
        - made
        - tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 0)
        - view-columns(loop, source.meta, source.columns)
        - loop
    put(made, tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 1), source.offset, loop)
    put-meta(loop, made, row-layout, 2, source.meta)
keep-state(slot, made, row, loop)
keep-state(slot + 1, source.length, types.size-type, loop)
. kind = intrinsic(type)
if facts.constant-of(unit.reading, loop) != no-fact && (kind == .table || kind == .table-span)
    . named = loop-name-slot(loop)
    if named != no-slot
        proven-items += ProvenItem(loop, named, source.columns)
= type

────────────────────
_ do hold-selection
    - loop SyntaxId
    - selection Operand
    - type TypeId
    - slot SlotId

` Begins a loop over a selection of a table's rows, as TypeScript's loop over rows begins it:
` the indices are resolved, then the table's columns and length found, checked where it
` grows. The selection is kept as a finished table of those columns and that length, read
` with no metadata, and, where the indices are not resolved again on each pass, with the
` indices where they lie; then the count of indices. A loop TypeScript leaves to the
` selection's own iteration is refused.
. constant = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, loop)
. reads = if constant != no-fact then facts.constants[constant].bits else 2u64
if reads == 2
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
. table-type = field-type(type, 0)
. span-type = field-type(type, 1)
. table-layout = layout-of(table-type, loop)
. span-layout = layout-of(span-type, loop)
. table = part(selection, layout, 0, loop)
. span = part(selection, layout, 1, loop)
. resolved = resolve-span(loop, span.operand, span-layout)
. source = table-source(loop, table.operand, table-type, table-layout)
. made = frame(layout)
copy(made, selection, layout, false, loop)
. kept-table = address(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 0).offset, table-layout, loop)
put-word(loop, kept-table, table-layout, 0, source.columns, pointer-layout)
put-word(loop, kept-table, table-layout, 1, source.length, u64-layout)
for position in 2 .. < tables.layouts.rows[table-layout].fields.count
    put-word(loop, kept-table, table-layout, position, integer(.machine-u64, 0), u64-layout)
if reads == 0
    . kept-span = address(made, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1).offset, span-layout, loop)
    put-word(loop, kept-span, span-layout, 0, resolved.data, u64-layout)
    put-word(loop, kept-span, span-layout, 1, integer(.machine-u64, 0), u64-layout)
keep-state(slot, made, type, loop)
keep-state(slot + 1, word-at(loop, span.operand, span-layout, 3), types.size-type, loop)

────────────────────
_ do read-selected Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId
    - done IRBlockId

` The next row of a loop over a selection of a table's rows, or a leave to `done` once the
` count read reaches the count of indices: the indices are resolved, again where the loop
` finds them on each pass, the index read at the count, and checked against the table's
` length as found when the loop began; the row there holds no metadata.
. none = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. item-slot = slot-offset(slot + loop-state-count - 1, loop)
. row = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, item-slot)
. row-kind = intrinsic(row)
if row-kind != .table-row && row-kind != .immutable-table-row
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(none, no-type)
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
. table-type = field-type(type, 0)
. span-type = field-type(type, 1)
. table-layout = layout-of(table-type, loop)
. span-layout = layout-of(span-type, loop)
. item = viewed-item(span-type)
. item-layout = layout-of(item, loop)
. row-layout = layout-of(row, loop)
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(loop, .compare-less, state(slot + 2, loop).operand, state(slot + 1, loop).operand), inside, done)
ir.start-block(inside)
. count = state(slot + 2, loop)
keep-state
    - slot + 2
    - arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, count.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 1), u64-layout)
    - types.size-type
    - loop
. selection = state(slot, loop)
. table = part(selection.operand, layout, 0, loop)
. span = part(selection.operand, layout, 1, loop)
. index = selected-index(loop, resolve-span(loop, span.operand, span-layout), count.operand, item, item-layout)
fail-if
    - loop
    - compare(loop, .compare-greater-equal, index, word-at(loop, table.operand, table-layout, 1))
    - "TableSelection index is out of bounds"
. made = frame(row-layout)
put-word(loop, made, row-layout, 0, word-at(loop, table.operand, table-layout, 0), u64-layout)
put(made, tables.layouts.field(row-layout, 1), index, loop)
for position in 2 .. < tables.layouts.rows[row-layout].fields.count
    put-word(loop, made, row-layout, position, integer(.machine-u64, 0), u64-layout)
= Typed(made, row)

────────────────────
_ do read-index Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId
    - done IRBlockId

` The next index of a loop over an index span, or a leave to `done` once the count read
` reaches the length read when the loop began: the span is resolved, and the index read at
` the count, as `s[i]` reads it.
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
. item = viewed-item(type)
. item-layout = layout-of(item, loop)
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(loop, .compare-less, state(slot + 2, loop).operand, state(slot + 1, loop).operand), inside, done)
ir.start-block(inside)
. count = state(slot + 2, loop)
keep-state
    - slot + 2
    - arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, count.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 1), u64-layout)
    - types.size-type
    - loop
. span = state(slot, loop)
. value = span-item(loop, resolve-span(loop, span.operand, layout), count.operand, item-layout)
= Typed(value, item)

────────────────────
_ reads-place Bool
    - loop SyntaxId

` Whether a loop reads its container where it is kept at each item, as the type pass
` planned it: in a function that yields the loop keeps the container, as the reference's
` does there, and so does the loop of a comprehension, which is given it.
!stepping && loop != given-loop && is-place-loop-plan(facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop))

────────────────────
_ do container-of Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId

` What a loop reads its items from: what it keeps, or its container read anew where it is
` kept, with the object it is a property of as that was when the loop began.
if !reads-place(loop)
    = state(slot, loop)
= emit-expression(written)

────────────────────
_ protocol-calls FactId
    - loop SyntaxId

` The calls the type pass recorded for the protocol of a loop, in the order the loop makes
` them: at the header of a loop, and for a bullet that gives every item of a container from
` the first the type pass kept for it, beside others where it kept them, as at a bullet that
` also keeps those of the first bullet of its list.
|? facts.bullet-site(unit.reading, loop) != loop || start != no-fact
    start
??
    facts.first-call(unit.reading, loop)

.. start = facts.protocol-start(unit.reading, loop)

────────────────────
_ do open-turn
    - loop SyntaxId
    - item Operand
    - type TypeId

` Starts a turn of a loop whose body declares a local that nested functions capture. The
` turn has an environment of its own: an object the collector owns, which arrives zeroed,
` with the link to the environment in force around the loop. A nested function written in
` the turn is given it, so that each turn's functions read that turn's locals. The item of
` the turn is copied there under each name it is captured by: the one the loop writes for
` it, `each` and `it`. A local holds the environment of the turn; in a function that
` yields, a field of the function's own environment does, which keeps it from one step to
` the next.
if unit.instance == no-instance
    =
. scope = tables.turn-scope(instances.rows[unit.instance].module, loop)
if scope == no-scope
    =
. layout = tables.turn-environment(unit.instance, scope)
if unit.reading != unit.instance || layout == no-layout || layout == unbuilt-environment
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
. place = if stepping then tables.turn-place(unit.instance, scope) else no-place
if stepping && (place == no-place || unit.environment == no-local)
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
. link = written-environment(loop)
. mark = pending.length
pending += integer(.machine-u64, tables.layouts.rows[layout].size)
pending += make-operand(.operand-descriptor, layout)
. made = call-runtime(.runtime-allocate-object, loop, mark, managed-layout)
. local = no-local
if stepping
    . field = tables.layouts.field(tables.environments[unit.instance], place)
    store(load-local(unit.environment, loop), field.offset, made, true, loop)
else
    local = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
    store-local(local, made, loop)
store(made, 0, link, true, loop)
open-turns += TurnScope(scope, local, place)
for offset in 0 .. < unit.slot-count
    . slot = unit.slot-start + offset
    . kind = bindings.slots[slot].kind
    if tables.slot-homes[slot] != scope
        continue
    if kind == .slot-each || kind == .slot-it || whole-item
        keep-captured(slot, item, type, loop)
    .. whole-item = kind == .slot-loop-item && facts.loop-take(unit.reading, loop) == .take-whole

────────────────────
+ do close-turns
    - mark Size

` Ends the turns opened since `mark`, where the body of their loop has been emitted.
while open-turns.length > mark
    open-turns.pop()

────────────────────
+ do loop-slots SlotId
    - loop SyntaxId

` The first of the slots the binder declared for what a loop keeps, in the function whose
` facts are being read, which is the one emitted.
. binding = instances.rows[unit.reading].binding
. slot = no-slot
if binding != no-binding && unit.reading == unit.instance
    slot = bindings.loop-state(binding, loop)
if slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
= slot

────────────────────
+ do emit-headed
    - first SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - clause SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId
    - kept Bool = false

` A loop over the container of each of its headers, by the protocol the type pass planned
` for each: by its indexes, by a cursor, or as a stream. A bullet that gives every item of
` a container is such a loop of one header, whose container the bullet keeps already (`kept`).
` 1. Every container is evaluated, in the order written, and then each is begun. From there
`    on, telling the streams among them that the loop has ended is a cleanup: it runs
`    however the loop is left, as the body of a `do finally` written there would.
` 2. A turn reads an item of each header in order. The head of a header polls and reads,
`    and a container with no more ends the loop. The header takes the item and tests its
`    clause; an item that does not match, or a `when` that fails, reads that header again.
` 3. The body runs. `continue` goes to the first head, as the end of the body does. The
`    body of a comprehension's loop is an expression, and is yielded, and a bullet has no
`    body and yields the item.
` In a cleanup being run, a check made in the loop lands where the cleanup ends, as in the rest
` of it, leaving its streams unended, as TypeScript's does (`end-in-cleanup`). A header that
` subscribes, the loop of a comprehension whose first header writes a pattern that is no match,
` and a stream read where the collector never looks have no shape.
. chain [SyntaxId]
. containers [SyntaxId]
. clauses [SyntaxId]
. streams = false
. header = first
. container = written
. tested = clause
while header != 0
    . plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, header)
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    do match? tree.nodes[header]
        | .node-loop-syntax(row)
            next = row.next
            if row.is-subscriber || (header == given-loop && !takes-item(header))
                refuse(.refused-statement, header)
    if plan == .plan-stream-loop
        streams = true
    else if !is-index-loop-plan(plan) && !is-cursor-loop-plan(plan) && other-loop-plan
        refuse(.refused-statement, header)
    .. other-loop-plan = plan != .plan-table-loop && plan != .plan-pattern-loop
    chain += header
    containers += container
    clauses += tested
    header = next
    do match? tree.nodes[header]
        | .node-loop-syntax(row)
            container = row.container
            tested = row.clause
. caught = landing
if streams && (is-free(unit.instance) || (scoping.cleaning && caught == no-block))
    refuse(.refused-statement, first)
    =
. pin-mark = pins.length
. slots [SlotId]
. kinds [TypeId]
. made = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    . slot = loop-slots(chain[position])
    . kind = hold-container(chain[position], containers[position], slot, kept && position == 0)
    made = holding
    slots += slot
    kinds += kind
protocol-row = U32.max
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    begin-items(chain[position], containers[position], slots[position], kinds[position])
. stream = U32.max
if chain.length == 1 && streams && !stepping && value-made
    stream = ir.streams.length as U32
    ir.streams.append(IRStream(made, protocol-row, U32.max, IdList()))
    stream-loops += first
.. value-made = operand-kind(made) == .operand-value || operand-kind(made) == .operand-argument
. mark = open-cleanups.length
. own-scoping = scoping
if streams
    scoping = scoping.block-base = mark
    open-cleanup(first, UseCell(no-local, no-local, no-type))
    if scoping.cleaning
        landing = caught
. root = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
. turns = open-turns.length
. depth = loops.length
. named = bound.length
. captured = stream-captures.length
. last = no-slot
jump(root)
. head = root
for position in 0 .. < chain.length
    . loop = chain[position]
    if position != 0
        head = ir.reserve-block()
        jump(head)
    ir.start-block(head)
    emit-poll(loop)
    . polled = ir.current
    protocol-row = U32.max
    . item = read-items(loop, first, containers[position], slots[position], kinds[position], done)
    if stream != U32.max
        ir.streams[stream].read = protocol-row
        ir.streams[stream].head = head
        ir.streams[stream].polled = polled
        ir.streams[stream].done = done
    . type = item.type
    last = slots[position] + loop-state-count - 1
    take-item(loop, last, item.operand, type, head)
    . turned = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, slot-offset(last, loop))
    loops += EmittedLoop(loop, root, done, item.operand, turned, open-cleanups.length, last)
    emit-clause(clauses[position], head, done)
if first == given-loop
    emit-yield(body, body, false)
else if tree.gives-items(first, body)
    give-item(first, facts.bullet-site(unit.reading, first), state(last, first))
else if body != 0
    emit-block(body)
close-turns(turns)
drop-bound(named)
drop-captures(captured)
while loops.length > depth
    loops.pop()
for ended in chain
    forget-item(ended)
jump(root)
ir.start-block(done)
if streams && scoping.cleaning
    end-in-cleanup(mark, caught)
else if streams
    close-cleanups(mark)
if streams
    scoping = own-scoping
unpin(pin-mark)

────────────────────
+ do end-in-cleanup
    - mark Size
    - caught IRBlockId

` Where a loop that reads a stream in a cleanup being run ends: its own cleanups run, newest
` first, and a check made in one lands where the cleanup around ends, as one made in the loop
` does. They are open no longer.
while open-cleanups.length > mark
    landing = caught
    run-cleanup(open-cleanups[open-cleanups.length - 1].body, open-cleanups[open-cleanups.length - 1].cell)
    open-cleanups.pop()
landing = caught

────────────────────
+ do begin-items
    - loop SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId

` Begins what a header of a loop reads its container by, once every container of the loop
` is held. By its indexes: the length is read once, by the getter the type pass recorded
` for it or as the field of an array a constant fact names, and the count of items read
` starts at none. By a cursor: the container gives the state the cursor starts at. As a
` stream: the container is told that the loop begins. As a stream pattern: the stream the
` pattern reads the container through is made and kept.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop)
if plan == .plan-table-loop
    keep-state(slot + 2, integer(.machine-u64, 0), types.size-type, loop)
    =
if plan == .plan-pattern-loop
    . held = state(slot, loop)
    . stream = stream-of(loop, held.operand, type, stream-maker(loop))
    keep-state(slot + 1, stream.operand, stream.type, loop)
    =
. begins = protocol-calls(loop)
if begins == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
if is-index-loop-plan(plan)
    . length = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    if facts.calls[begins].form == .call-getter
        length = call-protocol(loop, begins, container-of(loop, container, slot).operand, type, nothing)
    else
        length = array-length(loop, container-of(loop, container, slot).operand, type)
    if length.type != types.size-type
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
        =
    keep-state(slot + 1, length.operand, types.size-type, loop)
    keep-state(slot + 2, integer(.machine-u64, 0), types.size-type, loop)
    =
if is-cursor-loop-plan(plan)
    if facts.calls[begins].form != .call-getter
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
        =
    . started = call-protocol(loop, begins, container-of(loop, container, slot).operand, type, nothing)
    keep-state(slot + 1, started.operand, started.type, loop)
    =
. reads = facts.calls[begins].next
if reads == no-fact || facts.calls[reads].next == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
call-protocol(loop, begins, state(slot, loop).operand, type, nothing)

────────────────────
+ do read-items Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - place SyntaxId
    - container SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId
    - done IRBlockId

` Reads the next item of a header of a loop, where its head has polled, and leaves to
` `done` where its container has no more. By its indexes: the count of items read is tested
` against the length and moves on, and the item at the index it had is read by the
` container's `[]`. By a cursor: the container's function takes the state and gives the
` next with an item, or with none. As a stream: the container gives an item, or nothing,
` which is converted as the type pass said where a property the container delegates to gives
` it. As a stream pattern: the pattern matches once more on the stream kept for it.
` The calls are made at `place`, the loop's first header, where TypeScript makes the reads of
` every header.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop)
if plan == .plan-table-loop
    = read-row(loop, slot, done)
if plan == .plan-pattern-loop
    = read-step(loop, slot, type, done)
. begins = protocol-calls(loop)
if begins == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
if is-index-loop-plan(plan)
    . reads = if facts.calls[begins].form == .call-getter then facts.calls[begins].next else begins
    branch(compare(loop, .compare-less, state(slot + 2, loop).operand, state(slot + 1, loop).operand), inside, done)
    ir.start-block(inside)
    . index = state(slot + 2, loop)
    . moved = arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, index.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 1), u64-layout)
    keep-state(slot + 2, moved, types.size-type, loop)
    = call-protocol
        - place
        - reads
        - container-of(loop, container, slot).operand
        - type
        - index.operand
        - types.index-type
. next = nothing
. given = no-type
if is-cursor-loop-plan(plan)
    . offset = slot-offset(slot + 1, loop)
    . cursor = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset)
    . steps = facts.calls[begins].next
    . stepped = call-protocol
        - place
        - steps
        - container-of(loop, container, slot).operand
        - type
        - state(slot + 1, loop).operand
        - cursor
    . answer = stepped.type
    . layout = layout-of(answer, loop)
    if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout) || unpaired
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    .. unpaired = tables.layouts.rows[layout].fields.count != 2
    given = field-type(answer, 1)
    if field-type(answer, 0) != cursor
        refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    keep-state(slot + 1, take(stepped.operand, tables.layouts.field(layout, 0), loop), cursor, loop)
    next = take(stepped.operand, tables.layouts.field(layout, 1), loop)
else
    . answered = call-protocol(place, facts.calls[begins].next, state(slot, loop).operand, type, nothing)
    next = answered.operand
    given = answered.type
if !types.is-optional(given)
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
branch(present(loop, Typed(next, given)).operand, inside, done)
ir.start-block(inside)
= convert(loop, .reason-element, payload(loop, Typed(next, given)))

────────────────────
_ do read-step Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - type TypeId
    - done IRBlockId

` One pass of a loop whose header is a stream pattern, as the reference makes it: the stream
` kept for the loop is asked whether it has more, and the loop ends where it has not; it
` gives its view, and the pattern is matched from where the view starts, as a rule's arms
` are, without reading the rest, asking the stream for more input where a part reads past
` the end of its buffer. Where it passes, the stream commits where it ended, and the item is
` what it gives; where it fails, the stream commits where it started, and the loop ends.
` Where it passed without moving the stream on, it panics, as a pipe does. The names it
` captures stay bound for the body.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. pattern = tree.step-pattern(loop)
. result = if pattern != 0 then facts.node-type(unit.reading, pattern) else no-type
. made = stream-maker(loop)
. viewed = if made != no-fact then next-call(made) else facts.first-call(unit.reading, loop)
. commits = next-call(viewed)
. extends = next-call(commits)
. asks = next-call(extends)
if result == no-type || result == invalid-type || asks == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. stream = state(slot + 1, loop)
. stream-type = stream.type
. more = call-protocol(loop, asks, stream.operand, stream-type, nothing)
if more.type != types.bool-type
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. reading = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(loop, .compare-not-equal, more.operand, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), reading, done)
ir.start-block(reading)
. refills = made == no-fact || chunked
    .. chunked = same-decl(class-ref(types, stream-type), types.chunked-token-stream-decl)
. run = view-stream(loop, stream.operand, stream-type, refills, viewed, extends)
. value = attempt-arms(loop, pattern, result, run, false, commits, done, true)
=? value if value.type == no-type
. moved = ir.reserve-block()
. stuck = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(loop, .compare-greater, load-local(attempt-end, loop), run.start), moved, stuck)
ir.start-block(stuck)
raise-text(loop, "Stream pattern loop made no input progress")
ir.start-block(moved)
= value

────────────────────
+ stream-maker FactId
    - site SyntaxId

` The call the type pass recorded at a stream pattern or a loop's header that makes the
` stream it reads its subject through; none where the subject is a stream already.
if first != no-fact && facts.calls[first].form == .call-constructor then first else no-fact

.. first = facts.first-call(unit.reading, site)

────────────────────
_ do read-row Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - slot SlotId
    - done IRBlockId

` The next row of a loop over a table or a span of one, or a leave to `done` once the count
` read reaches the count of rows: the first row moved on by the count read.
. offset = slot-offset(slot, loop)
. row = facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset)
if intrinsic(row) == .table-selection || intrinsic(row) == .immutable-table-selection
    = read-selected(loop, slot, row, done)
if intrinsic(row) == .index-span
    = read-index(loop, slot, row, done)
. layout = layout-of(row, loop)
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(loop, .compare-less, state(slot + 2, loop).operand, state(slot + 1, loop).operand), inside, done)
ir.start-block(inside)
. count = state(slot + 2, loop)
keep-state
    - slot + 2
    - arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, count.operand, integer(.machine-u64, 1), u64-layout)
    - types.size-type
    - loop
. first = state(slot, loop)
. made = frame(layout)
copy(made, first.operand, layout, false, loop)
put
    - made
    - tables.layouts.field(layout, 1)
    - arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, part(first.operand, layout, 1, loop).operand, count.operand, u64-layout)
    - loop
= Typed(made, row)

────────────────────
+ do take-item
    - loop SyntaxId
    - last SlotId
    - item Operand
    - type TypeId
    - head IRBlockId

` What a header of a loop does with an item it has read, as the type pass decided. The item
` is kept in the last of the header's slots, where the body reads it. A turn whose locals
` nested functions capture gets an environment of its own. Then the header's pattern takes
` the item: one that names it whole does no more; one that writes names for the fields of a
` tuple takes it apart; one written as a match (`for | pattern in`) passes over an item it
` does not fit, and the header reads its next; and any other is one a declaration is
` written with, a type for the name or a pattern, which panics where the item does not fit.
` A match written with arms gives the body what the arm an item fits gives, as
` `take-matched` emits it. A comprehension's own loop that takes its item apart, and a
` pattern matched that is not written as a match, have no shape yet.
. take = facts.loop-take(unit.reading, loop)
. pattern SyntaxId = 0
. written SyntaxId = 0
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        written = row.pattern
        pattern = tree.matched-name(row.pattern)
if take == .take-arms
    take-matched(loop, written, pattern, last, item, type, head)
    =
keep-state(last, item, type, loop)
open-turn(loop, item, type)
if take == .take-whole
    =
if take == .take-unshaped || (pattern == written && (loop == given-loop || take == .take-fitted))
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
if take == .take-fields
    destructure(loop, tree.field-names(pattern), state(last, loop).operand, type, true, true)
    =
. held = state(last, loop)
. own-matching = matching
if take == .take-converted
    do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
        | .node-type-capture(capture)
            . given = convert(capture.type, .reason-declaration, Typed(held.operand, type), capture.id)
            matching = matching.declaring = true
            bind-name(capture.id, given)
            matching = own-matching
            =
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
if take == .take-declared
    shape-declared(loop, pattern, Typed(held.operand, type))
    =
. failed = ir.reserve-block()
. passed = ir.reserve-block()
matching = matching.declaring = true
emit-pattern(pattern, Typed(held.operand, type), failed)
matching = own-matching
jump(passed)
ir.start-block(failed)
jump(head)
ir.start-block(passed)

────────────────────
_ do take-matched
    - loop SyntaxId
    - match SyntaxId
    - arms SyntaxId
    - last SlotId
    - item Operand
    - type TypeId
    - head IRBlockId

` What a header whose pattern is the arms of a match does with an item it has read. The
` arms are tried on the item in the order written, and what the first that fits gives is
` the item of the turn, kept where the body reads it, in the type the type pass gave the
` arms. `it` in an arm is the item as read. An item no arm fits is passed over, and so is one
` whose arm gives an optional that holds nothing: the header reads its next.
. given = facts.node-type(unit.reading, match)
if given == no-type || given == invalid-type
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
. layout = layout-of(given, loop)
if layout == void-layout
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
. joined = ir.reserve-block()
. slot = join-slot(layout)
. mark = joins.length
. named = bound.length
. own-matching = matching
matching = matching.declaring = true
loops += EmittedLoop(loop, head, head, item, type, open-cleanups.length, no-slot)
. is-closed = match-arms(match, arms, item, type, given, given, joined, slot)
loops.pop()
matching = own-matching
drop-bound(named)
if !is-closed
    jump(head)
if operand-kind(slot) == .operand-void && joins.length == mark
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
. value = close-joins(joined, mark, layout, slot)
. kept = given
if types.is-optional(given)
    . passed = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(present(loop, Typed(value, given)).operand, passed, head)
    ir.start-block(passed)
    . inner = payload(loop, Typed(value, given))
    value = inner.operand
    kept = inner.type
keep-state(last, value, kept, loop)
open-turn(loop, value, kept)

────────────────────
+ do array-length Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - array Operand
    - type TypeId

` The length of an array a loop counts through: the field of it that the constant fact at
` the loop names.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. place = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, loop)
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
if place == no-fact || !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. position = facts.constants[place].bits as U32
if position >= tables.layouts.rows[layout].fields.count
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
= Typed(take(array, tables.layouts.field(layout, position), loop), field-type(type, position))

────────────────────
+ do end-streams
    - first SyntaxId

` Tells each container a loop reads as a stream that the loop has ended, in the order of
` its headers: the cleanup the loop opened where it began, emitted on each way out.
. header = first
while header != 0
    if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, header) == .plan-stream-loop
        end-stream(header)
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    do match? tree.nodes[header]
        | .node-loop-syntax(row)
            next = row.next
    header = next

────────────────────
+ do end-stream
    - loop SyntaxId

` Tells the container of a header that reads a stream that the loop has ended.
. slot = loop-slots(loop)
. held = state(slot, loop)
. type = held.type
. begins = protocol-calls(loop)
. reads = if begins == no-fact then no-fact else facts.calls[begins].next
if reads == no-fact
    refuse(.refused-statement, loop)
    =
call-protocol(loop, facts.calls[reads].next, held.operand, type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0))
for back in 0 .. < stream-loops.length
    . position = stream-loops.length - 1 - back
    if stream-loops[position] == loop
        ir.end-stream(position as U32, protocol-row)
        =

────────────────────
+ do emit-range-loop
    - loop SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - first SyntaxId
    - last SyntaxId
    - clause SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` A loop over a range of integers. Both ends are evaluated once, in the item's type. The loop
` counts up, or down when it starts above its end, which is decided once; one of an unsigned type
` that starts at a written 0 only counts up. A range written with
` `..` takes its end as an item and stops after it, and any other stops before its end. In
` a function that yields, the index, the end and the way it counts are kept in the loop's
` slots, and read again on each pass. The loop of a bullet that gives every item of a range
` has no body, and yields the item.
` 1. The head polls, then tests the index against the end.
` 2. Inside, the item is the index, the clause is tested, and the body runs.
` 3. The step ends the loop at an end the range takes, and otherwise moves the index.
. start = convert(first, .reason-element, emit-expression(first))
. type = start.type
. layout = layout-of(type, loop)
. counted = body != 0 && !stepping && !is-signed(layout) && range-plan && constant-bound
    .. range-plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, loop) == .plan-range-loop
    .. constant-bound = facts.constant-of(unit.reading, loop) != no-fact
. end = convert
    - last
    - .reason-element
    - if counted then counted-end(loop, last) else emit-expression(last)
if end.type != type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, loop)
    =
if !is-integer(layout) || !is-numeric-type(type)
    refuse(.refused-type, loop)
    =
if counted
    emit-counted-loop(loop, start.operand, end.operand, type, layout, clause, body)
    =
. wide = if tables.layouts.rows[layout].size >= 4 then layout else i32-layout
. rising = !is-signed(layout) && is-written-zero(first)
. falls = if rising then integer(.machine-u8, 0) else compare(loop, .compare-greater, start.operand, end.operand)
. pace = range-pace(loop, falls, wide, rising)
. index = no-local
. kept = no-slot
if stepping
    kept = loop-slots(loop)
    keep-state(kept, start.operand, type, loop)
    keep-state(kept + 1, end.operand, type, loop)
    keep-state(kept + 2, falls, types.bool-type, loop)
else
    index = ir.add-local(layout)
    store-local(index, start.operand, loop)
. head = ir.reserve-block()
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
. step = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
jump(head)

ir.start-block(head)
emit-poll(loop)
. takes-end = op == .range-through-op
if stepping
    end = state(kept + 1, loop)
    falls = state(kept + 2, loop).operand
. item = if stepping then state(kept, loop) else Typed(load-local(index, loop), type)
. below = if takes-end then .compare-less-equal else .compare-less
if rising
    branch(compare(loop, below, item.operand, end.operand), inside, done)
else
    . up = ir.reserve-block()
    . down = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(falls, down, up)
    ir.start-block(down)
    branch
        - compare(loop, if takes-end then .compare-greater-equal else .compare-greater, item.operand, end.operand)
        - inside
        - done
    ir.start-block(up)
    branch(compare(loop, below, item.operand, end.operand), inside, done)

ir.start-block(inside)
emit-loop-body(loop, item.operand, type, step, done, kept, clause, body)

ir.start-block(step)
if stepping
    item = state(kept, loop)
    end = state(kept + 1, loop)
    pace = range-pace(loop, state(kept + 2, loop).operand, wide, rising)
if takes-end
    . moving = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(loop, .compare-equal, item.operand, end.operand), done, moving)
    ir.start-block(moving)
. moved = num-cast
    - loop
    - arithmetic(loop, .arithmetic-add, num-cast(loop, item.operand, layout, wide), pace, wide)
    - wide
    - layout
if stepping
    keep-state(kept, moved, type, loop)
else
    store-local(index, moved, loop)
jump(head)
ir.start-block(done)
forget-proven(loop)

────────────────────
_ do range-pace Operand
    - loop SyntaxId
    - falls Operand
    - wide LayoutId
    - rising Bool

if rising
    = integer(wide as MachineKind, 1)
. rises = bitwise(loop, .bitwise-xor, falls, integer(.machine-u8, 1), u8-layout)
= arithmetic
    - loop
    - .arithmetic-subtract
    - num-cast(loop, rises, u8-layout, wide)
    - num-cast(loop, falls, u8-layout, wide)
    - wide

────────────────────
_ is-written-zero Bool
    - id SyntaxId

match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-integer-syntax(row)
        !row.unit && parse-integer-literal(row.value).value == 0
    ??
        false

────────────────────
_ do counted-end Typed
    - loop SyntaxId
    - last SyntaxId

do match? tree.nodes[last]
    | .node-get-expression(get)
        if table-plan && table-op(last) == TableOp.table-length && row-source
            . held = emit-expression(get.object)
            . type = held.type
            . layout = layout-of(type, last)
            . source = table-source(last, held.operand, type, layout)
            proven-tables += ProvenTable(loop, intrinsic(type), source)
            = Typed(source.length, types.size-type)
        .. table-plan = facts.plan-of(unit.reading, last) == .plan-table
        .. row-source = is-row-source(intrinsic(facts.node-type(unit.reading, get.object)))
= emit-expression(last)

────────────────────
_ do emit-counted-loop
    - loop SyntaxId
    - start Operand
    - end Operand
    - type TypeId
    - layout LayoutId
    - clause SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

. index = ir.add-local(layout)
store-local(index, start, loop)
. hoist = ir.reserve-block()
. head = ir.reserve-block()
. inside = ir.reserve-block()
. step = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
jump(hoist)

ir.start-block(head)
emit-poll(loop)
. item = load-local(index, loop)
branch(compare(loop, .compare-less, item, end), inside, done)

ir.start-block(inside)
emit-loop-body(loop, item, type, step, done, no-slot, clause, body)

ir.start-block(step)
. wide = if tables.layouts.rows[layout].size >= 4 then layout else i32-layout
. moved = arithmetic
    - loop
    - .arithmetic-add
    - num-cast(loop, item, layout, wide)
    - integer(wide as MachineKind, 1)
    - wide
store-local(index, num-cast(loop, moved, wide, layout), loop)
jump(head)

ir.start-block(hoist)
hoist-columns(loop)
jump(head)
ir.start-block(done)
forget-proven(loop)


────────────────────
_ do emit-loop-body
    - loop SyntaxId
    - item Operand
    - type TypeId
    - step IRBlockId
    - done IRBlockId
    - kept SlotId
    - clause SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` Emits a pass of a range loop over `item`, of `type`, which `continue` leaves for `step` and
` `break` for `done`: its clause, then its body, or where it has none and gives items, the item
` it gives.
. turns = open-turns.length
open-turn(loop, item, type)
loops += EmittedLoop(loop, step, done, item, type, open-cleanups.length, kept)
emit-clause(clause, step, done)
if tree.gives-items(loop, body)
    give-item(loop, facts.bullet-site(unit.reading, loop), read-item(loop, loop, type))
else if body != 0
    emit-block(body)
close-turns(turns)
loops.pop()
jump(step)
────────────────────
_ do hoist-columns
    - loop SyntaxId

. found = proven-loop(loop)
if found == U32.max
    =
. columns = proven-tables[found].source.columns
while proven-columns.length != 0 && proven-columns[proven-columns.length - 1].loop == loop
    . held = proven-columns[proven-columns.length - 1]
    store-local(held.local, load(columns, held.column * 8, pointer-layout, loop), loop)
    proven-columns.pop()

────────────────────
_ do forget-proven
    - loop SyntaxId

while proven-tables.length != 0 && proven-tables[proven-tables.length - 1].loop == loop
    proven-tables.pop()
. kept [ProvenRead]
for held in proven-reads
    if held.loop != loop
        kept += held
proven-reads.clear()
for held in kept
    proven-reads += held

────────────────────
_ do loop-name-slot SlotId
    - loop SyntaxId

. binding = instances.rows[unit.reading].binding
if binding == no-binding || unit.reading != unit.instance
    = no-slot
do match? tree.nodes[loop]
    | .node-loop-syntax(row)
        . identifier = row.pattern
        do match? tree.nodes[row.pattern]
            | .node-type-capture(capture)
                identifier = capture.id
        . resolution = bindings.resolution-of(binding, identifier)
        if resolution.kind == .resolve-slot
            = resolution.slot
= no-slot

────────────────────
_ do forget-item
    - loop SyntaxId

while proven-items.length != 0 && proven-items[proven-items.length - 1].loop == loop
    proven-items.pop()

────────────────────
+ do forget-read
    - loop SyntaxId
    - column U32

. kept [ProvenRead]
for held in proven-reads
    if held.loop != loop || held.column != column
        kept += held
proven-reads.clear()
for held in kept
    proven-reads += held

────────────────────
+ innermost-loop SyntaxId

if loops.length == 0 then 0 else loops[loops.length - 1].syntax

────────────────────
+ do emit-clause
    - clause SyntaxId
    - step IRBlockId
    - done IRBlockId

` The clauses of a loop, tested in the order written before its body on each pass. A `when`
` that fails goes on to the next pass. A `while` that fails ends the loop, and so does an
` `until` that holds. The first clause that decides wins: the clauses after it are not tested.
` A `whenever` says whether a loop on a stream is subscribed and is not tested here.
. current = first-tested(clause)
while current != 0
    . expr SyntaxId = 0
    . next SyntaxId = 0
    . passes = no-block
    . fails = no-block
    . resumed = ir.reserve-block()
    do match? tree.nodes[current]
        | .node-clause(row)
            expr = row.expr
            next = row.next
            do match? row.op
                | .when-clause
                    passes = resumed
                    fails = step
                | .while-clause
                    passes = resumed
                    fails = done
                | .until-clause
                    passes = done
                    fails = resumed
    if passes == no-block
        refuse(.refused-statement, current)
        =
    . tested = test(expr, emit-expression(expr))
    branch(tested.operand, passes, fails)
    ir.start-block(resumed)
    current = first-tested(next)

────────────────────
_ do first-tested SyntaxId
    - clause SyntaxId

` A clause, or the first written after it, that is tested before a loop's body: one that is not
` a `whenever`. None where there is none.
if clause == 0
    = 0
do match? tree.nodes[clause]
    | .node-clause(row)
        if row.op == .whenever-clause
            = first-tested(row.next)
= clause
